    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABOBohLw",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): per-api-key alias configurable rate limits",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 798,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nAdds `[rate_limit.alias_overrides.<alias>]` so individual authenticated aliases can get their own rate limits on top of `use_auth_alias`.\r\n\r\n- An alias that sets its own base (`base_rate` + `base_interval`, or `infinite_rate_limit = true`) uses only its own base and method overrides; global method overrides no longer apply to it.\r\n- An alias with only `method_overrides` keeps the global base and global method overrides, replacing or adding individual methods.\r\n- `infinite_rate_limit = true` on a per-alias method override leaves that method unlimited for the alias; `limit = 0` blocks it.\r\n\r\nInvalid configs fail at startup: overrides without `use_auth_alias = true`, aliases missing from `[authentication]`, conflicting or incomplete fields, non-positive base rates or intervals, negative method limits, and empty overrides.\r\n\r\nAlso fixes the README sentence from #761 that still described method quotas as additional to the base.\r\n\r\nUnchanged: IP-keyed limits, global `[rate_limit]` semantics, Origin/User-Agent exemptions, `global = true`, and the Redis key format.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\n- Unit tests for resolving the limits of each override shape, for validation (one row per error), and for choosing between override-alias, default-alias and IP limits.\r\n- Integration tests for each override shape with memory and Redis, a shared quota across two instances on one Redis, and startup failures.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-10T05:12:24Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-10T19:47:03Z",
      "additions": 705,
      "deletions": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABOHpH_g",
      "title": "ci: add agent approval check",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 799,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an `agent-approval-check` workflow that calls the reusable ethereum-optimism/factory `.github/workflows/agent-approval-check.yaml`, pinned to ethereum-optimism/factory@feec17f6a55c3bd2dd1f0f0459e942688489222f. It reports the `agent-approval-check` commit status on pull requests, reviews, `/approve` comments and merge groups. Pull requests authored by, approved by, or containing commits from agent and automation identities stay pending until two distinct human reviewers with write access approve the current head.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-10T13:55:45Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-10T15:36:22Z",
      "additions": 19,
      "deletions": 0
    },
